      "head": "# taskq-new — pyproject.toml\n#\n# Pin pytest discovery to the project test directory so the harness-side\n# pytest-cov and pytest-benchmark invocations do NOT collect\n# `harness/tests/*` (the vendored harness method library) from the project\n# root. Without this, `pytest` invoked bare from `/Users/johnny/projects/taskq-new`\n# collects the harness test suite alongside the project's own, and either\n# times out (pytest-cov at 120s) or fails collection (pytest-benchmark trips\n# on a harness test referencing fixtures that do not exist in this layout).\n#\n# See harness/core/quality_gate/cross_artifact.py:481 and the tool_runners\n# pytest invocation paths for why this matters at the gate level.\n#\n# `[tool.coverage.run]` scopes coverage measurement to the project's own\n# source tree. The harness invokes `pytest --cov=.` from the project root\n# (harness/core/quality_gate/cross_artifact.py:481); without a `source`\n# constraint that would measure everything under `.` — including the\n# vendored harness/, all of `.methodology/`, etc. — and blow past the\n# 120s budget on a 1000+ file tree. With `source = [\"03-development/src\"]`\n# coverage only instruments the project's actual source, so the run"
    },
